Lineage
-------

1. PyUltraLight (version 1), the original pseudo-spectral solver for
   ultralight dark matter dynamics:
   F. Edwards, E. Kendall, S. Hotchkiss and R. Easther,
   "PyUltraLight: A Pseudo-Spectral Solver for Ultralight Dark Matter
   Dynamics", JCAP 10 (2018) 027, doi:10.1088/1475-7516/2018/10/027,
   arXiv:1807.04037.
   PyUltraLight.py in this repository is a copy of that solver (not imported).

2. PyUltraLight 2 / PyUL_NBody: N-body particles, energy diagnostics, I/O
   management and the .uldm run files, by Yourong F. Wang and collaborators
   (Auckland Cosmology).
   Upstream repository: https://github.com/Sifyrena/PyUL_NBody
   Software record: Zenodo doi:10.5281/zenodo.6336160
   This repository is a fork of PyUL_NBody. Its git history up to and
   including commit 879b8e7 (25 June 2025; upstream PyUL 2.30.37 with its
   later patches) is the upstream history. PyUltraLight2/Previous.py is the
   upstream integrator PyUltraLight2/Current.py at that commit (S_version
   30.37), kept for reference (not imported).

3. SK fork (this repository), by Alan Zhang, from 29 January 2026 (commit
   039e05a onward): PyUltraLight2/Current_SK.py (cell-centred grids, manual
   dynamical friction, resampled centre-of-mass cube, and since 30.50 the
   portability, safety and bug fixes and the inline eigenmode decomposition
   listed in CHANGELOG.md), PyUltraLight2/_compat.py, the packaging, tests,
   examples and documentation.
   Repository: https://github.com/Ailun-Zhang/PyUL_SK

The upstream credits banner also acknowledges modules adapted from
J. L. Zagorac et al. (isolated potential, dispersive sponge) and from
N. Guo et al. (embedded-soliton profiles).

The SK fork was written for the black-hole simulations of
A. Zhang, Y. Wang, J. L. Zagorac and R. Easther, "Stone Skipping Black Holes
in Ultralight Dark Matter Solitons", arXiv:2602.11512 (2026),
https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.11512


